// Point.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > C-Struct Declaration, CStructs
//
// co.cstruct is a C-like value type: always copied on pass, simple memory
// layout, no metadata, safe to cross direct ABI and zone boundaries. This is
// the opposite of co.struct, which is passed by reference.
//
// Allowed field types: primitives (int, uint, float, bool, char, byte), fixed
// size arrays, and other cstructs.
//
// Forbidden: co.struct, co.string, dynamic bindings, classes,
// modules, any heap allocated type, methods, and associated functions.

_ co.cstruct = {
    x co.int;
    y co.int;
}
